BT /F2 10.50 Tf 53.00 685.89 Td (Introduction & Operational Context) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 659.89 Td (In Multi-Agent Robotic Systems \(MARS\) research, investigators must develop, deploy, and operate multiple robots) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 647.89 Td (concurrently. Compared with single-robot research, this introduces additional challenges associated with hardware) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 635.89 Td (maintenance, software development, system integration, and coordination among multiple agents.) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 619.39 Td (Based on practical experience operating a four-robot team, several platform requirements have been identified as) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 607.39 Td (particularly important for MARS research. These requirements extend beyond the fundamental capabilities of an) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 595.39 Td (individual mobile robot, addressing the additional complexity introduced by multi-agent interactions and fleet-level) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 583.39 Td (operations.) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 566.89 Td (A suitable research platform should prioritize reliability, modularity, ease of maintenance, and cost-effectiveness.) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 554.89 Td (These characteristics are essential for supporting long-term experiments, simplifying hardware and software) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 542.89 Td (development, and enabling researchers to scale their experiments by deploying larger numbers of robots within) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 530.89 Td (limited budgets.) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 514.39 Td (Furthermore, the platform should support both centralized monitoring and decentralized agent operation, allowing) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 502.39 Td (researchers to investigate different multi-agent architectures without being constrained by the underlying) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 490.39 Td (hardware infrastructure.) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 473.89 Td (Usability and accessibility should also be considered fundamental design objectives. Even in research laboratories) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 461.89 Td (with professional engineers and software developers, users should not be assumed to possess specialized knowledge) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 449.89 Td (across every discipline involved in robotics. Since robotics integrates multiple fields of engineering and computer) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 437.89 Td (science, operating and maintaining the platform should not require expertise in all of these areas. Therefore,) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 425.89 Td (adopting usability principles commonly found in commercial products, such as intuitive interfaces, straightforward) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 413.89 Td (configuration, accessible diagnostics, and simplified maintenance procedures, can significantly reduce the learning) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 401.89 Td (curve. This approach also makes the platform easier to transfer to other researchers and users, promoting) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 389.89 Td (reproducibility, collaboration, and long-term adoption.) Tj ET
