BT /F2 10.50 Tf 53.00 232.89 Td (1. Modularity and Extensibility) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 206.89 Td (Research objectives and interdisciplinary collaborations frequently introduce evolving hardware and software) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 194.89 Td (requirements. Therefore, the robot platform should adopt a modular architecture that accommodates) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 182.89 Td (modifications, component replacements, and the integration of additional hardware.) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 166.39 Td (A modular design promotes hardware and software reuse across different research projects, reducing) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 154.39 Td (development time and costs when establishing new experimental configurations. Furthermore, standardized) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 142.39 Td (mechanical interfaces, electrical connections, and communication protocols simplify system integration and) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 130.39 Td (maintenance as the fleet expands.) Tj ET
