BT /F2 10.00 Tf 106.73 730.89 Td (2.1 Power Regulation) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 712.89 Td (Lithium-based batteries are preferred because of their compact form factor and high energy density. However,) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 700.89 Td (battery voltage varies with the state of charge and instantaneous load conditions. Therefore, dedicated voltage) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 688.89 Td (regulation should provide stable supply voltages to critical electronic components and drive motors.) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 672.39 Td (Maintaining consistent motor supply voltage helps minimize variations in motor performance and preserve) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 660.39 Td (predictable motion characteristics across all agents.) Tj ET
