0.060 0.090 0.160 rg
BT /F2 10.00 Tf 106.73 575.89 Td (2.2 Battery Management and Protection) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 557.89 Td (Lithium-based batteries introduce operational hazards associated with overcharge, overdischarge, excessive) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 545.89 Td (current, and abnormal temperature conditions. An appropriate Battery Management System \(BMS\) should) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 533.89 Td (incorporate protection mechanisms to mitigate these risks.) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 517.39 Td (As the fleet size increases, the number of individual battery systems and associated failure points also increases.) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 505.39 Td (Therefore, integrated battery protection is essential for maintaining operational safety and reducing the risk of) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 493.39 Td (battery-related failures during experiments.) Tj ET
