0.060 0.090 0.160 rg
BT /F2 10.00 Tf 106.73 420.39 Td (2.3 Exchangeable Battery or Power Module) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 402.39 Td (The robot should support an exchangeable battery or power module to minimize downtime during experiments and) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 390.39 Td (simplify fleet maintenance. A modular power system allows researchers to replace depleted batteries quickly) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 378.39 Td (without waiting for individual units to recharge.) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 361.89 Td (The power module should incorporate standardized mechanical mounting and electrical interfaces to ensure) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 349.89 Td (compatibility across all robots in the fleet. Furthermore, the connection mechanism should provide secure) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 337.89 Td (attachment, correct polarity, and reliable electrical contact while allowing convenient removal and replacement. The) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 325.89 Td (design should also consider integrated battery protection and safe disconnection procedures to prevent electrical) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 313.89 Td (hazards during module replacement.) Tj ET
