0.060 0.090 0.160 rg
BT /F2 10.00 Tf 106.73 229.39 Td (2.4 Fleet Charging Infrastructure) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 211.39 Td (Charging a large fleet using individual battery chargers introduces considerable operational overhead and occupies) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 199.39 Td (valuable laboratory workspace. Therefore, the platform should support efficient fleet charging through centralized) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 187.39 Td (multi-port charging stations, shared power distribution systems, or automated docking stations.) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 170.89 Td (A standardized charging interface also simplifies battery maintenance and reduces the time required to prepare) Tj ET
0.180 0.230 0.300 rg
BT /F1 9.20 Tf 44.00 158.89 Td (robots for subsequent experimental runs.) Tj ET
